From ce801c564ce3ce2c0e44f382dc0e4ad7eb0f06ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:46:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar label gap: a setting for the space between icon and
 label

Upstream subtracts the icon's invisible margin from the label padding,
so larger home icons (home_icon_size_factor > 1) leave the label
touching the icon. New datastore float homar_label_gap_dp (default 0 =
upstream), declared in app/lawnchair/omalawn/HomarLabelGap.kt, adds its
dp to the workspace label padding (clamped to -8..32 dp; a negative
gap pulls the label closer to the icon).

Two hooks in DeviceProfile:
- getNormalizedIconDrawablePadding(), used only by the workspace
  branches (responsive, scalable, fixed), adds the gap before each
  branch fits the cell, so a short cell gives the space back from
  border spacing / cell padding.
- the fixed (non-scalable) grid clamps the padding to half the cell's
  free height, which goes negative when the cell is shorter than icon +
  label (4x8 with larger icons) and pulls the label into the icon by
  far more than needed. With a gap set, the padding becomes the wanted
  gap shrunk to the room the cell really has below icon and label,
  never below upstream's value, so the label is not cut.

On the fixed grid a negative gap takes its dp off upstream's padding.

All apps and folders keep their own padding; gap 0 is upstream exactly.

On Lawnchair 16 the label text factor is applied before the layout, so
the fixed-grid hook measures the label with the text size as it is.
